{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2577 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "25860a10c2c50524f2a6d0794a9bad190859a88cd10aab1a4554c9780c20ce05" :edb/db-before-t 2576 :edb/db-after-t 2577 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535889 50 #inst "2026-10-09T10:01:33.366Z" 13194139535889 true] [17592186096379 1100 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=3 \\\\ y+z=2 \\\\ z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535889 false] [17592186096379 1100 "Solve the following system of equations:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/assets/3b7ca238880ce9b06f58b1667d29b3fa0103560fa475238134cd3e802c7e7720.png)" 13194139535889 true] [17592186096380 1100 "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535889 false] [17592186096380 1100 "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/assets/1ecadec01586fecee4a8b6d8ad5015168387124430849ed2e7d884908e28e927.png)" 13194139535889 true] [17592186096380 1145 "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/assets/c7c7d0904aa85c2cd9915e95a8ca3cee9857deb216148f59372204c6672d8811.png)\n\nThe third equation states that $x_3=5.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(5)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-5=-7.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 5$ and $x_2 = -7$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx_1+(-7)-(5) = 1\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = 1 + 7 + 5 = 13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 13,$ $x_2=-7,$ and $x_3 = 5.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 13,-7,5 \\rangle.$" 13194139535889 true] [17592186096380 1145 "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{3}=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $x_3=5.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(5)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-5=-7.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 5$ and $x_2 = -7$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx_1+(-7)-(5) = 1\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = 1 + 7 + 5 = 13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 13,$ $x_2=-7,$ and $x_3 = 5.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 13,-7,5 \\rangle.$" 13194139535889 false] [17592186096381 1100 "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535889 false] [17592186096381 1100 "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/assets/fd5c0fe6de60e36b0bd2414cb8ef991265c30bdfa4d8cfdac3242f51a54dbb87.png)" 13194139535889 true] [17592186096381 1145 "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/assets/41347eb5694181e386cae05a31e455d12e2fbd1a0d70cd36bb37ed72da75f82d.png)\n\nThe third equation states that\n\n$$\n3x_3=3 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \n\tx_3=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(1)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-1=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 1$ and $x_2 = -3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x_1+(-3)-(1) = 0\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = \\dfrac{1}{2} (3 + 1) = 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 2,$ $x_2=-3,$ and $x_3 = 1.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 2,-3,1 \\rangle.$" 13194139535889 true] [17592186096381 1145 "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ 3{x}_{3}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that\n\n$$\n3x_3=3 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \n\tx_3=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(1)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-1=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 1$ and $x_2 = -3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x_1+(-3)-(1) = 0\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = \\dfrac{1}{2} (3 + 1) = 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 2,$ $x_2=-3,$ and $x_3 = 1.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 2,-3,1 \\rangle.$" 13194139535889 false] [17592186096590 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372700 13194139535889 true] [17592186096590 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372707 13194139535889 true] [17592186096590 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372714 13194139535889 true] [17592186096590 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372721 13194139535889 true] [17592186096590 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372728 13194139535889 true] [17592186096591 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372735 13194139535889 true] [17592186096591 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372756 13194139535889 true] [17592186096592 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372742 13194139535889 true] [17592186096592 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372749 13194139535889 true] [17592186096592 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372763 13194139535889 true] [17592186096844 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535889 true] [17592186096844 1100 "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139535889 false] [17592186096844 1100 "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535889 true] [17592186096844 1145 "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=1 \\\\  & y+z=1 \\\\  & z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(1)=1\\,⟹\\,y=1-1=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=1$ and $y=0$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(0)+(1)=1\\,⟹\\,x=1-1=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=0$, $y=0$, and $z=1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨0,0,1⟩.$" 13194139535889 true] [17592186097097 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535889 true] [17592186097097 1100 "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535889 true] [17592186097097 1100 "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139535889 false] [17592186097097 1145 "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say,  ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=5 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\  & {x}_{3}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(2)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-2$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(-2)+4(2)=5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=5-6-8=-9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=-9$, ${x}_{2}=-2$, and ${x}_{3}=2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨-9,-2,2⟩.$" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372700 1017 #edb/ref 17592186372701 13194139535889 true] [17592186372700 1089 "q-10196" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372700 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535889 true] [17592186372700 1100 "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1 \\\\  & {x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\  & {x}_{3}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372700 1113 #uuid "0eaafb8d-a24a-511f-876f-5fa5e395d49d" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372700 1145 "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=3.$ Substitute this into the second equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-(3)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-1+3=2.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=2$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(2)+(3)=1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1-3+2=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=0$,  ${x}_{2}=2$, and ${x}_{3}=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨0,2,3⟩.$" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372702 13194139535889 true] [17592186372701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372703 13194139535889 true] [17592186372701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372704 13194139535889 true] [17592186372701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372705 13194139535889 true] [17592186372701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372706 13194139535889 true] [17592186372701 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535889 true] [17592186372701 1041 "selection" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372701 1104 #edb/ref 17592186372706 13194139535889 true] [17592186372701 1110 #uuid "0e95e61c-82d3-5ae9-bc50-9d01f4d743de" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372702 1034 "⟨1,3,2⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372702 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186372702 1111 #uuid "ec9e3dfd-6d35-5ac5-bd17-acd8a11964b8" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372703 1034 "⟨0,3,-2⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372703 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186372703 1111 #uuid "dcf5cf11-c5e8-5cf5-a35a-49d716e9112c" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372704 1034 "⟨1,-3,2⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372704 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186372704 1111 #uuid "a3d81afe-921f-5924-8ec4-3752eef4e765" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372705 1034 "⟨1,-3,0⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372705 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186372705 1111 #uuid "0edc8e80-301c-592b-85cd-1b34f987523f" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372706 1034 "⟨0,2,3⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372706 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186372706 1111 #uuid "e9ef19ec-6bc1-523f-8c3b-2651dab6090b" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372707 1017 #edb/ref 17592186372708 13194139535889 true] [17592186372707 1089 "q-10197" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372707 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535889 true] [17592186372707 1100 "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-y-z=4 \\\\  & y+2z=2 \\\\  & z=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372707 1113 #uuid "bb9885ea-e95d-568e-b27f-f6fb8125bfd9" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372707 1145 "he third equation states that  $z=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+2(\\frac{1}{2})=2\\,⟹\\,y=2-1=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $y=1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx-(1)-(\\frac{1}{2})=4\\,⟹\\,x=4+1+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{11}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{11}{2}$,  $y=1$, and $z=\\frac{1}{2}.$  In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨\\frac{11}{2},1,\\frac{1}{2}⟩.$" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372709 13194139535889 true] [17592186372708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372710 13194139535889 true] [17592186372708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372711 13194139535889 true] [17592186372708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372712 13194139535889 true] [17592186372708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372713 13194139535889 true] [17592186372708 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535889 true] [17592186372708 1041 "selection" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372708 1104 #edb/ref 17592186372712 13194139535889 true] [17592186372708 1110 #uuid "50a17234-e53b-5a7c-8b1f-09c832529c88" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372709 1034 "⟨\\frac{9}{2},2,\\frac{1}{2}⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372709 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186372709 1111 #uuid "5f3317f9-68bb-50ce-b85a-970c07f76819" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372710 1034 "⟨\\frac{9}{2},1,2⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372710 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186372710 1111 #uuid "6bd7cd63-d162-562a-b09a-b624c1bc386f" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372711 1034 "⟨1,\\frac{9}{2},-\\frac{1}{2}⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372711 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186372711 1111 #uuid "a8651e20-cac5-5bfc-a19f-fe299eea69b6" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372712 1034 "⟨\\frac{11}{2},1,\\frac{1}{2}⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372712 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186372712 1111 #uuid "02a3e13b-ed4d-50a8-8598-03cb46de040c" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372713 1034 "⟨\\frac{1}{2},-1,2⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372713 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186372713 1111 #uuid "5b068c12-9e64-5004-93f2-2a94cf0badb4" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372714 1017 #edb/ref 17592186372715 13194139535889 true] [17592186372714 1089 "q-10198" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372714 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535889 true] [17592186372714 1100 "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=9 \\\\  & {x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=2 \\\\  & {x}_{3}=\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372714 1113 #uuid "8bfbf7d4-d461-5ae8-bd89-a3d95042e1da" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372714 1145 "The third equation states that  ${x}_{3}=\\frac{1}{3}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-3(\\frac{1}{3})=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=2+1=3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=\\frac{1}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(3)+3(\\frac{1}{3})=9\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=9+3-1=11.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=11$, ${x}_{2}=3$, and ${x}_{3}=\\frac{1}{3}.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨11,3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩.$" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372716 13194139535889 true] [17592186372715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372717 13194139535889 true] [17592186372715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372718 13194139535889 true] [17592186372715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372719 13194139535889 true] [17592186372715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372720 13194139535889 true] [17592186372715 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535889 true] [17592186372715 1041 "selection" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372715 1104 #edb/ref 17592186372719 13194139535889 true] [17592186372715 1110 #uuid "c39b8b99-6b9b-567e-ac99-c783d05d4941" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372716 1034 "⟨9,2,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372716 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186372716 1111 #uuid "69b3a22a-5c15-5091-82dc-c5e6b98642bb" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372717 1034 "⟨12,-3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372717 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186372717 1111 #uuid "a1ae9096-d25e-5cb5-9b03-ce33265a6f76" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372718 1034 "⟨9,-3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372718 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186372718 1111 #uuid "d0166eab-0786-56ff-9710-3df80a8ba13c" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372719 1034 "⟨11,3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372719 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186372719 1111 #uuid "20fdd5e8-0c68-5e8f-a2e2-d0c30071d9e3" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372720 1034 "⟨11,3,3⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372720 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186372720 1111 #uuid "b7fd4a74-59cb-5c43-a370-5f85e656f676" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372721 1017 #edb/ref 17592186372722 13194139535889 true] [17592186372721 1089 "q-129447" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372721 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535889 true] [17592186372721 1100 "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & {x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372721 1113 #uuid "5e5b828c-ff83-5c0f-9142-19fd4fcaac5d" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372721 1145 "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-1)=-\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}+1=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${x}_{3}=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(\\frac{1}{2})+(-1)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2+1+1=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=4$, ${x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}$, and ${x}_{3}=-1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨4,\\frac{1}{2},-1⟩.$" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372722 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372723 13194139535889 true] [17592186372722 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372724 13194139535889 true] [17592186372722 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372725 13194139535889 true] [17592186372722 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372726 13194139535889 true] [17592186372722 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372727 13194139535889 true] [17592186372722 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535889 true] [17592186372722 1041 "selection" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372722 1104 #edb/ref 17592186372724 13194139535889 true] [17592186372722 1110 #uuid "f5a75cdc-4e49-5bb1-bb5f-984866609910" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372723 1034 "⟨0,-\\frac{3}{2},-1⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372723 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186372723 1111 #uuid "f5659597-6148-5340-9cce-da4d3d90a594" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372724 1034 "⟨4,\\frac{1}{2},-1⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372724 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186372724 1111 #uuid "89884620-80a8-5e42-aa60-587cf8de4fc1" 13194139535889 t