d by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372763 1113 #uuid "c1d6feb3-6a84-59ca-8e6c-8c1a5c040ca0" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372763 1145 "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+y+z=-1 \\\\  & y+z=1 \\\\  & 2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that\n \n\n$$\n2z=1\\,⟹\\,z=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(\\frac{1}{2})=1\\,⟹\\,y=1-\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=y=\\frac{1}{2}$  into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x+(\\frac{1}{2})+(\\frac{1}{2})=-1\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}(-1-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2})=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-1$, $y=\\frac{1}{2}$, and $z=\\frac{1}{2}.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨-1,\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}⟩.$" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372765 13194139535889 true] [17592186372764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372766 13194139535889 true] [17592186372764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372767 13194139535889 true] [17592186372764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372768 13194139535889 true] [17592186372764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372769 13194139535889 true] [17592186372764 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535889 true] [17592186372764 1041 "selection" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372764 1104 #edb/ref 17592186372768 13194139535889 true] [17592186372764 1110 #uuid "43fd12c1-dcef-5689-8821-3f9dd4c9b252" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372765 1034 "⟨1,\\frac{1}{2},1⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372765 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186372765 1111 #uuid "09196d8a-0f6e-5f17-bd63-e3c5edc5079a" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372766 1034 "⟨-1,\\frac{1}{2},-1⟩" 13194139535889 true] [17592186372766 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535889 true] [17592186